{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "04", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "07", "M": "33", "S": "22"}}, "news": [{"title": "Visakhapatnam civic body to streamline building permissions, water supply connections", "para": "In a recent meeting, GVMC's chief city planner A Prabhakar Rao assured developers that the town planning department is actively resolving building permission issues. This includes streamlining the application process for greater efficiency. Superintending engineer Pallam Raju addressed water supply connection procedures, while developers voiced concerns that officials responded to, elaborating on regulations and timelines for future projects. GVMC is committed to providing ongoing support to builders and developers.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/visakhapatnam-civic-body-to-streamline-building-permissions-water-supply-connections/134669680?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-18410/134669680.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "New housing launches slow as developers in Goa turn cautious", "para": "In Panaji, the launch of new residential projects is stalled as developers grapple with escalating construction costs and uncertain regulations. Following a post-pandemic boom, the market is now experiencing reduced sales and growing unsold inventory. Local buyers are feeling the squeeze, with affordability declining despite stagnant prices. Some developers are opting to hold off on new ventures until clearer policies emerge, though a handful remain hopeful about future market dynamics.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/new-housing-launches-slow-as-developers-in-goa-turn-cautious/134669653?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-925329/134669653.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Pune: Yerawada MHADA residents protest stalled redevelopment, demand mini-clusters", "para": "Residents of Yerawada are voicing dissatisfaction with the halted redevelopment project by MHADA, advocating for the creation of smaller housing clusters. They argue that the current mega-cluster proposal fails to ensure the necessary resident agreement, affecting over 3,500 homes. Their recent protest demonstrates a pressing need for faster solutions to unsafe living conditions.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/pune-yerawada-mhada-residents-protest-stalled-redevelopment-demand-mini-clusters/134669598?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-585880/134669598.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}